Tests in-place freelist design, constant-time ops, and alignment in a tiny allocator. It also probes corruption handling with simple sanity checks.

## Key Concepts
- In‑place free-list within blocks
- Fixed-size allocator, O(1) operations
- 64-byte blocks, 8-byte alignment, cache considerations
- Simple corruption checks and thread-safety implications

